session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress: plan-review certified (b1e5fe91b4b), claimed. Implemented TDD on branch s2-reclaim-publish, commit 61223a0aa67: src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py (stamp_superseding_epoch, publish_git_ref, rollback_git_ref, publish_s3_bundle_set), compat.store_epoch_problem lineage relaxation, docs/concurrency.md paragraph, tests/unit/test_reclaim_publish.py + tests/integration/test_reclaim_publish_s3.py (10 tests, RED first then green; existing epoch-guard and stale-override suites still pass). lint, typecheck, ratchets green. make verify running before Gerrit push.","timestamp":1794874389313566137},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify on b2e19d1b827: first run surfaced a real fixture-policy finding (test_bare_clone_source_upkeep_sweep: the test created its bare remote by hand without upkeep pins; and test_bare_repository_fixture_portability: it addressed the bare remote via -C). Fixed by using _git_upkeep.init_bare_remote and a --git-dir helper. Rerun: default tier 21338 passed, integration tier 222 passed, exit 0. Pushed as Gerrit change 3409 (hashtag rebar-session-3d705fec).","timestamp":1794879531153072189}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788046507255058770,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5effac1e-f66e-4588-b502-561786bad344","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"aff9-1252-ad21-4695"},{"link_uuid":"b09dce85-db4b-457e-bae9-876a9a9174b9","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bdf3-e7e3-c96f-4b9f"},{"link_uuid":"21bf545e-b1e7-4946-a89a-b3d25da691bc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"237f-8d63-0dae-43ce"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nS1 (`filmable-crushing-nighthawk`, `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py:63` `collapse_shadow_tracker`) produces a rewritten below-horizon baseline in a disposable shadow clone. This story builds the **publish-swap** that would replace the published `tickets` history with that baseline, and the **rollback** that would restore it, both behind one precondition: replace only if the remote is unchanged since T0, else abort with no write. ADR 0106 §6 (`docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md:126-135`) requires a git-ref CAS on git remotes and an exclusive bundle-set replacement on the `git-remote-s3` backend, because the S3 auto-doctor (`src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py:62` `heal_multi_bundle`) folds divergent heads into a lossless merge and would resurrect the replaced history. Nothing executes a real swap here; the S3 dry-run story and a human go/no-go drive it later.\n\n## Approach\n\nOne new library module, `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py`, with no CLI verb (the S3 dry-run harness is its only caller). Every entry point first calls S1's shadow guard `_assert_shadow_tracker` (`reclaim_collapse.py:200`), which refuses anything without the `.rebar/reclaim-shadow-clone` marker, with a configured remote, or equal to the live tracker. Pushes go to an explicit remote URL argument, so the shadow never needs a named remote.\n\n- **Epoch stamp.** `stamp_superseding_epoch(shadow, new_epoch, replaced_tip=\"HEAD\")` commits, on the shadow's HEAD, the store-compat record of `replaced_tip` re-stamped with `compat.superseding_record` (`src/rebar/_store/compat.py:291`, merged with `sarcastic-specified-kodiakbear` in 9099c548247). Clones on the replaced history then prove supersession through `compat.remote_epoch_supersedes_local` and take the stale-clone override in `src/rebar/_store/stale_override.py`.\n- **git ref remotes** (bare, GitHub, Gerrit): `publish_git_ref` runs ONE `git push --atomic --force-with-lease=refs/heads/<branch>:<T0> <url> <new>:refs/heads/<branch> <T0>:refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-<stamp>`. The same push creates the backup ref at T0 and moves the branch; a moved branch fails the lease and the atomic push writes neither ref (`PublishAborted`).\n- **S3** (`git-remote-s3`, ADR 0093): `publish_s3_bundle_set` takes the helper's per-ref lock (`acquire_lock`, as `s3_doctor.heal_multi_bundle` does), asserts the bundle-head set (`get_bundles_for_ref`, sha from the key) equals the T0 set or aborts, copies every original bundle to `<prefix>/<ref>/PROTECTED#rollback-<stamp>/` (keys the helper's enumeration already skips), writes one bundle of the new tip, deletes the originals, calls `init_remote_head`, and releases the lock in `finally`. The doctor is never called.\n- **Rollback re-convergence.** `rollback_git_ref` publishes a restored tip under a lease on the rewritten tip. The restored tip is the backup tip plus a stamp with `replaced_tip=<rewritten tip>`, so its lineage names both the original and the rewritten epochs. Clients already on the rewritten baseline see unrelated history with a superseding epoch and are overridden back (aff9's protocol). Clients that never moved share history with the restored tip; for them `compat.store_epoch_problem` (`compat.py:200`) is relaxed to allow the union when the remote lineage names the local epoch, so their unpushed writes merge instead of being refused.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py` (new): stamp, git-ref publish, git-ref rollback, S3 bundle-set publish.\n- `src/rebar/_store/compat.py`: `store_epoch_problem` accepts a remote whose lineage names the local epoch.\n- `tests/unit/test_reclaim_publish.py` (new): git-ref adapter and rollback re-convergence against throwaway bare remotes.\n- `tests/integration/test_reclaim_publish_s3.py` (new): S3 adapter against `tests/integration/s3_doctor_harness.py`'s `FakeS3Remote`.\n- `docs/concurrency.md`: a short \"Publishing a reclaimed baseline\" paragraph next to aff9's reconnect protocol.\n\n## Testing\n\nTDD, red first; all repositories are throwaways under `tmp_path`, S3 is the fake.\n\n- git ref happy path: branch moves to the new tip and `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-*` holds T0.\n- git ref failure: a writer pushes after T0; the swap raises `PublishAborted` and the remote branch and backup namespace are unchanged.\n- Shadow guard: a plain clone (no marker) is refused.\n- Rollback: a client that moved onto the rewritten baseline is overridden back onto the restored tip; a client that never moved keeps its unpushed event merged on top of the restored tip; a rollback whose lease is stale aborts with no write.\n- S3 happy path: exactly one bundle remains and clones to the new tip; each original's bytes exist under the rollback prefix; the lock is released.\n- S3 failures: a head set different from T0 aborts with the object directory byte-for-byte unchanged; a held lock aborts with no write.\n- Doctor bypass: running `heal_multi_bundle` after the swap is a `noop` and T0 is unreachable from the published tip.\n- `pytest tests/integration/test_reclaim_publish_s3.py -m integration` is run explicitly in addition to `make verify` (whose integration tier also selects it).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The git-ref adapter swaps via `--force-with-lease` and aborts with no write when the remote moved since T0, verified on a throwaway bare remote by `tests/unit/test_reclaim_publish.py`.\n- [x] The S3 adapter performs a push-locked bundle-set replacement that asserts the T0 head set, backs up bundles to a rollback prefix, writes one rewritten bundle, deletes the originals, and is not merged back by the auto-doctor, verified on the fake-S3 fixture by `tests/integration/test_reclaim_publish_s3.py`.\n- [x] A backup ref (git) or rollback bundle prefix (S3) is captured before the first destructive step in each adapter, asserted by the same tests.\n- [x] The rollback re-convergence path is documented in `docs/concurrency.md` and covered by a fixture in which a client on the rewritten baseline is overridden back onto the restored ref.\n- [x] `make verify` is run and any failure is fixed or shown environmental (it passes when rerun in isolation or outside the agent sandbox); the Gerrit change gets `Verified +1`; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exit 0.\n- [x] [non-codebase] No real `tickets` remote is swapped by this story; all evidence comes from `tmp_path` repositories and the fake S3 remote.\n  provenance: environment=developer-workstation-worktree; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=static-analysis — the story adds library code and tests whose every swap and push targets a tmp_path repository or the fake S3 remote, and no swap is executed against any real store.\n\n## Portability\n\nBoth adapters use core-git ref primitives (`push --atomic --force-with-lease`, `bundle create`) or the store's existing `git-remote-s3` seam; nothing depends on a CI provider.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py","reason":"New: epoch stamp, git-ref publish/rollback with atomic lease push, S3 exclusive bundle-set publish."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"store_epoch_problem accepts a remote whose epoch_lineage names the local epoch (rollback re-convergence)."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reclaim_publish.py","reason":"RED-first git-ref adapter, lease abort, shadow guard, and rollback re-convergence tests."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_reclaim_publish_s3.py","reason":"RED-first S3 adapter tests on the FakeS3Remote fixture, including the doctor-bypass check."},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"Document publishing a reclaimed baseline and rollback re-convergence."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","aff9-1252-ad21-4695"],["depends_on","bdf3-e7e3-c96f-4b9f"],["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","237f-8d63-0dae-43ce"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"627dc